The structure templates in this folder are copied from data/dungeonnowloading/structures/ in that jar:
the corridors of its labyrinth and the labyrinth rooms at most 32 blocks on an axis. Each room's YAML
sidecar names its source file.

Changed by Realmforge (2026-10-14), with `rf rooms import` and the rules in
art/rooms/dungeon_now_loading/rules.yaml of the Realmforge repository:
- minecraft:chain renamed to minecraft:iron_chain and minecraft:grass to minecraft:short_grass, their
  names in current Minecraft;
- the marker blocks its processor list generic_degradation replaces when the labyrinth generates set to
  what it always or nearly always picks (red wool and black glass to stone, the other glass and carpets
  to air);
- Dungeon Now Loading's own blocks replaced by vanilla blocks that look alike (wall torches, banners,
  barrels, pointed dripstone for its spikes, spruce slabs for its wall platforms) or removed (pebbles,
  wall racks, and the blocks that run its mechanics);
- jigsaws inside a room (decorations, spawners, rewards) replaced by the block they leave behind, and
  the connectors renamed realmforge:door (sides) and realmforge:shaft (up, down);
- the containers' loot tables and every entity except item frames removed;
- more block variety added (mossy, cracked and gravel variants on plain floors, walls and ceilings) and
  decorations (vines, cobwebs, barrels, armor stands on stone brick stairs);
- templates written back in a normalized form (blocks sorted, stored deflate).
